<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzhhorod</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ungvár</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uzhhorod is a city on the Uzh river in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, the administrative centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Zakarpattia</a> Oblast on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>. Long part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, it gave its name to the Union of Uzhhorod of 1646, which brought the region's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> clergy into union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. It was the capital of Subcarpathian Ruthenia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> took it in 1938.</p></div>
